test-suites	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-08T02:29:51.7123812Z === issue #2190: the router binds the internal network only ===
test-suites	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-08T02:29:51.7125491Z   PASS: the sidecar is created on the internal network, so that is the only address it has at start-up
test-suites	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-08T02:29:51.7127119Z   PASS: with the alias tasks use, which the bind script resolves to find that address
test-suites	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-08T02:29:51.7128837Z   PASS: the router image is entered through sh, because router serve has no bind-to-network option yet
test-suites	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-08T02:29:51.7129784Z   PASS: sh is handed the bind script as its command
test-suites	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-08T02:29:51.7130385Z   PASS: and that script is the constant the real-Docker probe validates
test-suites	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-08T02:29:51.7130960Z   PASS: no port is published to the host
test-suites	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-08T02:29:51.7131474Z   PASS: the script looks up its own internal address by alias
test-suites	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-08T02:29:51.7132144Z   PASS: and binds that address alone on the port gh expects api.github.com on
test-suites	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-08T02:29:51.7132991Z   PASS: when the alias does not resolve the script refuses rather than fall back to every interface
test-suites	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-08T02:29:51.7133644Z   PASS: so no branch of it ever asks for 0.0.0.0
test-suites	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-08T02:29:51.7134157Z   PASS: and that refusal ends the container, which acquire reports as unhealthy
test-suites	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-08T02:29:51.7134685Z   PASS: the upstream network defaults to the docker bridge
test-suites	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-08T02:29:51.7135483Z   PASS: which is the network with a route to the vendor APIs
test-suites	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-08T02:29:51.7135946Z   PASS: an operator may name another network with egress
test-suites	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-08T02:29:51.7136626Z   PASS: but naming the internal network is ignored: it has no egress and would leave the router with no upstream at all
test-suites	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-08T02:29:51.7164896Z   PASS: a fresh sidecar comes up against a healthy fake docker
test-suites	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-08T02:29:51.7166426Z   PASS: the upstream bridge is connected after the container was created on the internal network
test-suites	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-08T02:29:51.7167326Z   PASS: and before health is probed, so an unhealthy verdict is never caused by a missing upstream
test-suites	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-08T02:29:51.7168190Z   PASS: health is probed through the internal alias, the only address the router now answers on
test-suites	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-08T02:29:51.7168921Z   PASS: loopback is never probed: the router does not bind it any more
test-suites	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-08T02:29:51.7169484Z   PASS: a router created on the internal network is kept
test-suites	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-08T02:29:51.7196902Z   PASS: a bridge that is already attached counts as attached, so re-acquires against a running router succeed
test-suites	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-08T02:29:51.7214012Z   PASS: a router that cannot reach its upstream is reported rather than handed to a task
test-suites	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-08T02:29:51.7215689Z   PASS: and no token is issued on it
test-suites	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-08T02:29:51.7216572Z   PASS: the routeless container is removed, so the next acquire starts clean
test-suites	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-08T02:29:51.7217427Z   PASS: the primary network of a legacy container reads as the bridge
test-suites	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-08T02:29:51.7224629Z   PASS: acquiring against a legacy router succeeds
test-suites	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-08T02:29:51.7225859Z   PASS: by replacing it: the legacy container is removed and a new one created on the internal network
test-suites	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-08T02:29:51.7226655Z   PASS: and the operator is told why the router restarted
test-suites	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-08T02:29:51.7243730Z   PASS: first task takes a lease (this recreates the legacy router)
test-suites	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-08T02:29:51.7252696Z   PASS: a second task still gets a token
test-suites	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-08T02:29:51.7253617Z   PASS: but a legacy router with a live lease is not restarted under the task holding it
test-suites	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-08T02:29:51.7254364Z   PASS: the restart is deferred and announced instead
test-suites	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-08T02:29:51.7271870Z   PASS: reading the primary network of a missing container yields null rather than throwing into acquire
